{
  "name": "Service Account Used Interactively",
  "description": "Backup service account svc_bkp_prod was supposed to run cron jobs only. A sysadmin needing fast access borrows the credentials and uses them for an interactive RDP session into a Windows file server, then opens PowerShell and pokes around.",
  "reasoning": "AD as the auth source, a Windows file server as the destination. The detection signal is 'svc_*' account showing a Logon Type 10 (RemoteInteractive) where it has only ever shown Type 5 (Service) before.",
  "category": "insider",
  "difficulty": "medium",
